===============================================================================================================================

docker -v                  = to check the docker installed version.
docker pull                = pull the docker command from the docker hub.
 ex : docker pull lerndevops/myapp01:sampleapp-v1

docker ps                      = used to list all active, currently running Docker containers on your system.
docker image ls                = to list all the downloaded image.
ex : nginx:stable-alpine3.24           0985e772fb9f       93.6MB           27MB    U

sudo usermod -aG docker ubuntu(username of vm)      =  The command sudo usermod -aG docker ubuntu adds the user ubuntu to the docker supplementary group.
                                                      This permits that user to run Docker commands without needing to prefix them with sudo.

docker image inspect image:version                  = to inspect any image 
ex : docker image inspect nginx:stable-alpine3.24
ex : docker image inspect tomcat:8.5.1

docker image rm image:version  = to delete the image.
ex: docker image rm nginx:stable-alpine3.24
ex: docker image inspect tomcat:8.5.1

docker container ls             =   to check if any container is running.
docker ps -a                    =   check container in hidden mode.
docker stop my-container        = to stop container.

